# Git LFS is for large binaries whose every revision would otherwise sit in the
# pack forever, downloaded by everyone. It is deliberately NOT used for text.
#
# A config file in LFS is unreadable in a pull-request diff, needs a round trip
# to inspect, and is invisible to grep-based checks -- which is how an internal
# experiment path hid inside resolved_configs.yaml until LFS payloads were
# materialised. Those sidecars are 0.6-56 KB; keeping them in the pack costs
# about 21 MB against a 312 MB history and buys back reviewability.

# Arrays, tensors and model weights
*.npy filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.npz filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.pkl filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.pt filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.ckpt filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.onnx filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Geometry and scenes
*.obj filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.stl filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.usd filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.usda filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.blend filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.blend1 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.fbx filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Media
*.gif filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.mp4 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# PNG is deliberately absent, and should stay absent. Two of the four PNGs in
# the repository are runtime assets the simulator loads -- a 2 KB checkerboard
# texture and a 2.5 KB terrain grid. In LFS those become pointer stubs in any
# clone made without LFS, and in every clone of every repository in the
# organisation if the shared LFS bandwidth quota is ever exhausted, which would
# break asset loading for a few kilobytes of nominal saving. All four PNGs come
# to 2.1 MB.
#
# If a genuinely large texture set arrives later, add it by path, the way the
# motion lists below are, rather than by extension. An extension-wide rule is
# what swept the small config sidecars into LFS in the first place.

# Bulk motion lists only. These reach 7 MB and churn with the motion set, so
# they earn their place. Everything else under data/ that happens to be YAML,
# JSON or CSV stays in the pack on purpose.
data/yaml_files/*.yaml filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
